     {"issue": "The instruction that \"Student and parent must determine the age of legal competency to sign contracts, in the state of the student's residence\" shifts an undefined legal determination to the signers without saying what follows if the determination is wrong. \"Minor (under 18 years of age in most states)\" is itself hedged and leaves the class of persons who must obtain a parent signature uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
