   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The definition of \"inherent risks\" as those \"which cannot be eliminated without destroying the unique character of the activities\" is a standard whose boundary must be applied case by case, and the list is expressly non-exhaustive (\"among others\", \"some, but not all\"). Whether a particular accident was an \"inherent\" risk is exactly the kind of question a court is asked to construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
